  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/... \nA much quieter period of weather is anticipated starting Tuesday\nas the flow turns more out of the west southwest ushering much\ndrier air through the rest of the area. Forecast PWATs are\nexpected to drop to just below normal on Tuesday, likely staying\non the lower side through around Thursday. NBM PoPs drop off to \nmostly below 10% starting Tuesday and carrying through at least \nWednesday. Temperatures will also be a bit slow to warm back up as\nthe trough will still have some influence over our region. \nForecast highs return back into the normal range by Wednesday, \nwhile overnight lows will be a more comfortable upper 70s to low \n80s for the lower deserts.\n\nHigh model uncertainty becomes an issue late week into next \nweekend as models are currently favoring a tropical cyclone to\nmove northwestward off the coast of Baja and potentially even\ngetting close to California early during the following week. It is\nimpossible to know at this point where this TC will go, but it at\nleast seems fairly likely it will help to direct moisture\nnorthward into our region by next weekend. Assuming this occurs,\nwe may eventually return to busy monsoon weather.",
